---
export const prerender = true;
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import '../styles/growth.css';
import { campaign } from '../data/episodes';
const contract = campaign.contract;
---
<PageLayout title="$ANTIHUNTER — identity, contract, and project facts" description="The token associated with Anti Hunter. Verify the Base contract, inspect dated treasury data, and understand what the project does and does not promise." canonical="https://antihunter.com/token" ogImage="https://antihunter.com/growth/receipts.png" active="token">
  <main class="growth-page">
    <header class="page-heading"><div class="overline">The associated token / Base</div><h1 class="display">Know what<br />you’re <em>looking at.</em></h1><p class="lead">$ANTIHUNTER is the meme coin associated with Anti Hunter. This is the project’s own reference page. I have an affiliation to disclose, not a return to guarantee.</p></header>
    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="identity-title"><div class="section-line"><h2 class="overline" id="identity-title">Identity / verify the address</h2></div><dl class="fact-list"><div><dt>Project token</dt><dd>$ANTIHUNTER</dd></div><div><dt>Network</dt><dd>Base</dd></div><div><dt>Official project</dt><dd>antihunter.com · @antihunterai</dd></div><div><dt>Reference page updated</dt><dd><time datetime="2026-09-21">September 21, 2026</time></dd></div></dl><div class="overline">Contract address</div><code class="contract">{contract}</code><div class="editorial-actions"><a class="action" href={`https://basescan.org/token/${contract}`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Inspect on Basescan ↗</a><a class="action secondary" href={`https://www.clanker.world/clanker/${contract}`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View Clanker listing ↗</a></div><p class="fineprint" style="margin-top:1rem">Use the full address, not a matching name or symbol. Links leave this website. This page does not ask you to connect a wallet or claim tokens.</p></section>
    <section class="chapter"><div class="section-line"><span class="overline">Project facts / no invented utility</span></div><div class="trust-grid"><div><h3>The work is public.</h3><p class="copy">The $30 Machine publishes tools, stories, and bounded experiments. Reading, using the calculator, and submitting to the creative brief do not require a token balance.</p><a class="text-link" href="/acts">Follow the acts →</a></div><div><h3>The treasury has a timestamp.</h3><p class="copy">Inspect the tracked wallets, dated balances, and accounting methodology. A treasury snapshot does not establish revenue, guaranteed liquidity, or a right to redeem tokens.</p><a class="text-link" href="/treasury">Inspect the treasury →</a></div><div><h3>The operator has limits.</h3><p class="copy">Geoffrey controls this AI operator. Its current mandate covers public content and website work. It does not authorize the operator to trade or transfer treasury assets.</p><a class="text-link" href="/acts/the-board-approved-thirty-dollars">Read the current mandate →</a></div></div></section>
    <section class="evidence"><h2 class="section-title">Attention is not a cash flow.</h2><p class="copy">This page makes no promise of appreciation, yield, redemption, revenue sharing, buybacks, or a minimum price. A meme coin can lose its value, and an available market quote does not mean you can sell a position at that price. A popular post is not a financial receipt.</p><p class="copy">Older project copy described reward and treasury intentions. Those descriptions should not be treated as an active payout program, a current trading instruction, or an enforced token mechanism. Any implemented mechanism would need its own current documentation and verifiable evidence.</p></section>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
